### External Geographic Data & Upstream Attributions

OpenUBEM interacts with, processes, and downloads geographic features, cadastral registries, meteorological datasets, and building physics models. These third-party datasets and tools are not covered by the OpenUBEM license itself and remain subject to their respective upstream licenses and attribution terms:

- **OpenStreetMap (OSM)**: © OpenStreetMap contributors, licensed under the [Open Data Commons Open Database License (ODbL)](https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/).
- **Cadastral & National GIS Registries**:
  - **Spain**: Sede Electrónica del Catastro — Licencia de uso general de datos catastrales abiertos.
  - **France**: IGN BD TOPO / Cadastre — [Licence Ouverte (Etalab 2.0)](https://www.etalab.gouv.fr/licence-ouverte-open-licence/).
  - **United Kingdom**: Ordnance Survey (OS Open Map Local) / HM Land Registry — [Open Government Licence v3.0 (OGL)](https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/).
  - **Austria**: Stadt Wien Open Data / Geoland — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
  - **Canada**: Ville de Montréal / Données Québec — Licence des données ouvertes de la Ville de Montréal.
  - **Armenia, Finland, Hungary, Italy**: Respective national cadastral and municipal open data registers.
- **ERA5 Climate Data**: Generated using Copernicus Climate Change Service (C3S) information [2026].
- **EnergyPlus**: Developed by the National Renewable Energy Laboratory (NREL), U.S. Department of Energy, under BSD-3-Clause.
